From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:30:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,sn2400-charger: Add
 read-only properties

A board being brought up may need its SN2400 charger left as the
bootloader set it. The iPhone 6s Plus has the iPhone 7's SN2400, but its
iOS driver never programs the battery charge-current limit. Describe
both opt-ins: apple,read-only for a board whose charger may only be
read, apple,keep-charge-limit for one whose charge limit stays as the
bootloader set it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/apple,sn2400-charger.yaml  | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,sn2400-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,sn2400-charger.yaml
index 6ec7a7147..034380cf7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,sn2400-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,sn2400-charger.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,18 @@ properties:
     description:
       Maximum USB input current that the foldback policy may request.
 
+  apple,read-only:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Only read the charger and leave it as the bootloader programmed it. For
+      boards whose charging policy has not been tested yet.
+
+  apple,keep-charge-limit:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Leave the battery charge-current limit as the bootloader set it, for
+      boards whose iOS driver never programs it.
+
   mux-states:
     maxItems: 1
 
